# Code Review Standards

## Review Dimensions

| Dimension | Weight | Focus |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| Correctness | 30% | Logic, edge cases, error handling |
| Architecture | 25% | Pattern compliance, boundary respect |
| Testing | 20% | Coverage, quality, edge cases |
| Security | 15% | Input validation, auth, secrets |
| Performance | 5% | Obvious issues, N+1, bundle size |
| Maintainability | 5% | Naming, comments, complexity |

## Severity Levels

| Level | Definition | Action |
|-------|------------|--------|
| 🔴 BLOCKER | Security vulnerability, data loss, crash in critical path | Must fix before merge |
| 🟡 MAJOR | Logic error, architectural violation, missing tests | Must fix, can discuss timeline |
| 🟢 MINOR | Style issue, nitpick, suggestion | Author's discretion |
| 💡 SUGGESTION | Idea for future improvement | Non-blocking |

## Checklists by Change Type

### API Changes
- [ ] Contract updated in .jules/contracts/api-contracts.md
- [ ] Backward compatible or versioned
- [ ] Error responses documented
- [ ] Rate limits considered
- [ ] Authentication required where appropriate

### Database Changes
- [ ] Migration is reversible
- [ ] Index added for foreign keys
- [ ] No N+1 query introduced
- [ ] Data integrity preserved
- [ ] Rollback tested

### UI Changes
- [ ] Responsive design verified
- [ ] Accessibility (a11y) checked
- [ ] Loading states handled
- [ ] Error states handled
- [ ] Cross-browser compatible

### Dependency Changes
- [ ] License compatible
- [ ] Security audit passed
- [ ] Bundle size impact assessed
- [ ] Alternatives considered

## Code Quality Gates

| Gate | Threshold | Enforcement |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Test coverage | 80% minimum, 90% critical paths | CI block |
| Lint | Zero errors, warnings justified | CI block |
