| Duplication | < 3% | Review flag |

PHASE 3 — FAULT PATTERNS:

Document in .jules/review/fault-patterns.md:

# Common Fault Patterns to Catch

## Logic Errors
- Off-by-one errors in loops
- Null/undefined dereferencing
- Race conditions in async code
- Incorrect boolean logic (De Morgan violations)
- Missing break in switch statements
- Floating point equality checks

## Architecture Violations
- Backend importing frontend code
- Frontend directly accessing database
- Service bypassing API contracts
- Circular dependencies
- Leaking implementation details across layers

## Security Anti-Patterns
- Hardcoded secrets or credentials
- SQL injection (string concatenation)
- XSS (unescaped user input)
- Insecure randomness for security
- Missing authentication checks
- Incorrect authorization (checking role vs permission)

## Performance Issues
- N+1 database queries
- Unbounded result sets
- Synchronous I/O in async context
- Memory leaks (uncleared intervals, event listeners)
- Large bundle imports (importing all of lodash)
- Missing debounce on rapid events

## Testing Gaps
- No test for error conditions
- No test for boundary values
- Mocking implementation instead of interface
- Tests that don't actually assert
- Flaky tests (timing-dependent, random data)

## Maintainability Issues
- Magic numbers without constants
- Deep nesting (> 3 levels)
- Functions > 50 lines
- Classes with > 10 methods
- Inconsistent naming conventions
- Missing or misleading comments

